LEAKAGE ATTRIBUTION -- measured, not assumed
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
A distractor class names the lever it was BUILT to bait. That label is a
design intention. The column that matters is the measured one: which
lever actually carries the bait above the records it displaces. Where
they differ, read the leakage count above as naming the DOMINANT lever,
not the class name.

bait                             class                   labelled     dominant lever   swing
d10_reflection_weight_bait       reflection_weight_bait    +0.621    A_T-off_scoring  +0.621
d07_lexical_overlap_bait         lexical_bait              +0.033            A_H-off  +0.143
d03_decay_old_recipe             decay_bait                +0.000      A_quality-off  +0.050
d04_decay_old_travel             decay_bait                +0.000      A_quality-off  +0.050
d02_typeboost_weather            type_boost_bait           +0.230        A_decay-off  +0.858
d06_recency_today_plant          recency_bait              +0.309        A_decay-off  +0.720 *
d12_lexical_overlap_bait_recent  lexical_bait              +0.060      A_quality-off  +0.212
d08_entity_name_bait             entity_bait               +0.124            A_H-off  +0.151
d01_typeboost_grocery            type_boost_bait           +0.179            A_H-off  +0.445

  * recency and decay are NOT separable by construction, and no corpus
    can make them so. Both key on the same input -- the record's age --
    but act on opposite sides of the pair: the additive freshness bonus
    lifts the fresh distractor, and the multiplicative decay penalty
    pushes down the older relevant record it displaces. A fresh bait is
    helped twice by two mechanisms a minimal pair cannot tell apart,
    because holding age constant disables both at once. That is a
    property of the pipeline, not a limit of these fixtures, and it is
    printed rather than tuned away.

